{% extends '@CitadelAureum/core/docs/layout.html.twig' %}

{% block article %}
    <p>
        Bars is the directory staff use when guests ask "where should we go
        for a drink?": a curated list of bars nearby, organised by style, with
        dress codes, happy hours, whether they take walk-ins or reservations,
        and opening times.
    </p>

    <h2>Common tasks</h2>
    <ol class="au-docs-steps">
        <li>Open <strong>Directory → Bars</strong> and filter by style, tag, dress code or entry policy.</li>
        <li>
            Check the open/closed indicator in the first column, or click it
            for the full week's opening times. The column can be sorted to
            bring places that are open now to the top.
        </li>
        <li>With manage permission, add new bars or update details when happy hours, dress codes or opening hours change. Where the hotel has Google sync enabled, hours can be filled in and refreshed automatically.</li>
        <li>Link an event to a bar from the events calendar to flag a deal or event on the day.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="au-docs-note">
        <i class="ph ph-info"></i>
        <p>
            Anyone who can view the module can browse; adding and editing
            bars, bar styles and tags needs manage permission. Tags are shared
            with Restaurants.
        </p>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
